  "_comment_residual": "Documented residuals: contact text the rule deliberately does not catch -- digits spelled out or swapped for look-alike letters, internal notes written in plain English, internal notes written in plain English, internal notes written in plain English, internal notes written in plain English, internal notes written in plain English, and a suite word before a dash pair whose second number has no leading zero. Both engines must still ALLOW each one, so a change to any of them is visible; the human review before a seal is their control. An access code written before its trigger word (\"4411 at the gate\") is a documented residual: the rule reads a trigger word, then the digits. A seven-digit local number with a comma between its groups (\"555, 0100\"), after a dollar sign (\"$555 0100\"), split 3-2-2 (\"555 01 00\") or followed by an area or count unit (\"Call 555 0100 sf\") is a documented residual: a comma makes a list, a dollar sign a price and a unit a measure.",
